# .privacy-forbidden.example
#
# Copy this file to .privacy-forbidden.local and fill in your real private values.
# .privacy-forbidden.local is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
#
# One forbidden string per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# These strings will be searched in PDF metadata and body text.
# When a match is found the script reports the file but does NOT print the term itself.
#
# ── Private legal name ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PRIVATE_LEGAL_NAME_HERE
#
# ── Private email address ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PRIVATE_EMAIL_HERE
#
# ── Old GitHub username (if private) ─────────────────────────────────────────
OLD_USERNAME_HERE
#
# ── Local machine / hostname ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOCAL_MACHINE_NAME_HERE
#
# ── Any other private identifier ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add one per line below this comment.
